###############################################################################
# Q10 -- Benchmark results
###############################################################################

# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training ran on a single node with 8 Nvidia H100 80GB GPUs; the complete
# training cost is stated as 400 to 700 GPU hours from the smallest to the
# most complex model (kept as text in trainingHardware because the figure
# is not attributed to a single training stage). Table II gives MD
# throughput in microseconds/atom/step on four GPU types; the A100 column
# is recorded as inferenceHardware on the five -OMAT models.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Validation is by MatBench Discovery F1, kappa-SRME, elastic constants, and grain-boundary, surface and point-defect formation energies; none is an energy/force/stress error on a material system, so no AccuracyMetric is encoded.
# - Table S2 (distillation of fine-tuned models into GRACE-FS on HEA25S, with energy and force errors) and the fine-tuning study of Fig. 8 are not encoded.
# - Table S1 also lists a 1L-medium configuration; no model of that configuration is named in the benchmark tables, so it is not encoded.
# - Each -OMAT model is the result of two stages (OMat-base, then 2 more epochs with alpha_E : alpha_F : alpha_S = 128 : 128 : 256); the run encodes the base-stage epochs and learning rate and names the second stage in its label. The -OAM models start from the OMat-base weights, which schema 0.1.2 cannot express.
# - lmax = 4 is encoded as mlips:numAngularBasis and the product order 4 as mlips:bodyOrder, following the reading used for MACE and CACE.
# - Other foundation models compared in the paper (ORB-v3, SevenNet-MF-ompa, MatterSim, MACE-MPA-0, MACE-OMAT-0, eSEN, DPA-3.1) are evaluated on benchmark scores and throughput only and are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
